[Event "Knight School"]
[Opening "Open Games (1...e5)"]
[Variation "Philidor Defense: Légal Trap"]
[ECO "C41"]
[Character "tactical"]
[Risk "high"]
[EarlyMate "white"]
[Tricks "trap,pin,mate-threat"]
[Themes "legal-mate,poisoned-queen"]
[For "black"]
[Kind "against-us"]
[Opponent "3...d6 4.Nc3 Bg4 5.Nxe5"]
[Start "giuoco-piano 3.Bc4"]

3... d6 $6 { Playable, but the quiet 3...d6 invites a pin with ...Bg4, and that is how Légal's mate happens. 3...Bc5 develops more actively and avoids it. } 4. Nc3 Bg4 $6 { Pins the knight on f3 to the queen. Pinning against Nc3 and Bc4 allows a famous trick. } 5. Nxe5 $1 { White leaves the queen en prise on purpose. } 5... Bxd1 $4 { Taking the queen is the losing mistake. If Black simply takes the knight on e5 first, White is the one in trouble. } 6. Bxf7+ { Check! The bishop attacks the king. } 6... Ke7 7. Nd5# *
